.TH id 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
id \- print user and group identity
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B id
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B id
prints the real user and group ids, with their names from
.B /etc/passwd
and
.BR /etc/group ,
and the effective ones where they differ.
.SH OPTIONS
None.  There is no
.BR \-u ,
.B \-g
or
.BR \-n ;
use
.BR whoami (1)
for the effective user name alone.
.SH NOTES
FUZIX has no supplementary group list, so there is nothing for a
.B groups
line to show.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR whoami (1),
.BR logname (1),
.BR who (1)
